# Arctic Wolves Video Companion Server - Environment Configuration
# Copy to .env and set the encryption key below. That is the ONLY
# required environment variable.
#
# The companion is a worker/integration service for the main Arctic Wolves
# application.  It handles hardware-accelerated video transcoding to HLS.
#
# All other settings (API key, RustFS credentials, main app URL, hardware
# acceleration method, etc.) are entered through the companion web UI at
# http://localhost:5100 → Settings and stored in an AES-256-CBC encrypted
# config file on the persistent Docker volume (/config).
#
# ── Setup flow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Set the ENCRYPTION_KEY below (must match the main application).
#   2. Start the container: docker compose up -d
#   3. Visit http://localhost:5100 → Settings.
#   4. Click "Generate API Key" — copy the key.
#   5. Enter the generated key in the main app under Game Plan Settings →
#      Companion Server → API Key.
#   6. In the main app's RustFS settings, click "Push to Companion" to
#      send the S3/RustFS connection credentials automatically.
#
# Storage paths (where videos live, where HLS output goes) are controlled
# entirely by the main application — it tells the companion exactly where
# each source file is and where to write the transcoded output.

# ── Encryption Key (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# AES-256-CBC key used to encrypt the persistent config file.
# Must match the ENCRYPTION_KEY in the main application's arctic_wolves.env
# so both apps use the same PII encryption scheme.
# Generate with: python -c "import os; print(os.urandom(32).hex())"
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
